{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018355-artifact-help","id":1018355,"title":"Artifact Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-16T22:58:38-08:00","id":1018355,"title":"Artifact Help","content":"This question is a bit more in-depth, so I wanted to have room to discuss rather than post it in the simple questions thread.<br /> <br /> I am building an Artifact for a Relic Attuned Sleepwalker rather than a Mage.<br /> <br /> It has two effects.<br /> <br /> One: When it touches a Mage, it casts Channel Mana to refill itself. As I understand, this gives the Artifact Prime 3 for rolling dice and sets the base cost to 3. The Reach will be used for Instant casting.<br /> <br /> Two: When it touches a non-Mage, it casts Wards and Signs upon the target. This should increase the cost to 4. For another dot, I can add a Utility Attainment. I'd like to add Time in a Bottle so that I can spend Mana to cast instantly so that the Reach is free to use Advanced Duration (and the other Reach probably for Advanced Potency). Conditional Duration takes it to 6 dots, with a (probably &quot;infrequent&quot;) Condition of &quot;when the Artifact is removed&quot;. &quot;Common&quot; seems more accurate for &quot;removing the artifact,&quot; but it feels really cheese.<br /> <br /> A total cost of five dots should mean Gnosis 3 and 12 Mana stored.<br /> <br /> Questions:<br /> <br /> One: Do Artifact effects have a base Mana cost of 1 like Imbued Items do? That is, will Channel Mana cost 0 or 1 Mana? Will Wards and Signs cost 1 or 2 Mana? It's a bigger deal for Channel Mana, given it's my only way to refill the thing barring finding a willing Mage to donate.<br /> <br /> Two: When is the spell cast? If someone touches it in combat, does Channel Mana get cast on their turn or mine? Does it take my action? I imagine not, but it can't hurt to ask.<br /> <br /> Three: Can you adjust the Spell Factors? Do you have to do so when creating the Artifact, or can it be done every time the spell is cast? I'm mostly concerned about the fairly unimpressive Potency 3 for Channel Mana, meaning it's unlikely to ever steal so much as a single point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T05:29:04-08:00","id":1018429,"title":"","content":"1. No, they do not. That's one of the biggest benefits of Artifacts over Imbued Items<br /> 2. When you cast it. Artifact usage involve the casting of a spell, with Paradox, deciding spell factors and reach, and everything.<br /> 3. Yes, see 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T07:14:06-08:00","id":1018448,"title":"","content":"My only issue there is that the Merit states that the Artifact uses its effects upon a trigger. That doesn't sound like &quot;when you cast it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every Artifact will use its effects under different circumstances,<br /> determined when you create the Artifact. For example, an Artifact<br /> might cast its effect the moment it is first seen by human eyes, or<br /> whenever it\u2019s dropped on the ground. </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the response, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T08:42:04-08:00","id":1018467,"title":"","content":"The trigger causes the artifact to cast it, usually the person using the artifact is causing the trigger to occur, so effectively the user is casting via the artifact.<br /> <br /> A different way to look at that, is that you the player roll the casting dice pool for the artifact, so when -you- cast it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T11:16:06-08:00","id":1018516,"title":"","content":"Do you have to buy Utility Attainments once per effect, or once for the entire Artifact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}